# Act II
dialogue quill
  node root quill "You're the clerk. Licence and everything. Don't get comfortable."
    > "I'm crew now." -> crew
    > "I need to see the captain." if not quill_helped -> captain
    > "You must be the lookout who spots lies at two miles." if seen:tavernkeeper.crew and not seen:quill.marta -> marta
    > "I found your spyglass." if has spyglass and seen:quill.what -> lost
    > "What's ahead of us?" -> ahead
    > "Nothing. Carry on." -> bye
  node crew quill "Crew is what the captain writes in the book. You're cargo with opinions."
    > "I need to see the captain." if not quill_helped -> captain
    > "Fair enough." -> bye
  node marta quill "Marta. Of course. Did she mention compliments?"
    > "(Say nothing.)" -> learn
      add aff 1
    > "She said you bite." -> bite
  node learn quill "Good. You learn fast, for cargo."
    > "I need to see the captain." if not quill_helped -> captain
    > "I'll leave you to the horizon." -> bye
  node bite quill "Only cargo. Keeps the weight down."
    > "I need to see the captain." if not quill_helped -> captain
    > "Noted. From a safe distance." -> bye
  node captain quill "She's aft. Past me. Crew only, and see above regarding cargo."
    > "What would get me past?" -> what
    > "I found your spyglass." if has spyglass and seen:quill.what -> lost
    > "I'll find a way." -> bye
  node what quill "Be useful. Or find my spyglass. I dropped it somewhere on deck in the dark last watch, and I've been squinting at the horizon like a mole with ambitions."
    > "Is this it?" if has spyglass -> lost
    > "I'll keep an eye out." -> bye
  node lost quill "That's mine. Where did you… never mind. Give it here, and I'll forget I ever saw a clerk aft of the mast."
    > "Here. (give the spyglass)" -> thanks
      take spyglass
      set quill_helped
      note quill_spyglass "Quill dropped her spyglass on deck in the dark and would not let a clerk past without it. Returning it bought me the run of the aft deck."
    > "Not yet." -> bye
  node thanks quill "There she is. Dented twice, still honest. …You're blurrier up close. Go on, then. Captain's down the companionway at the stern."
    > "Thank you, Quill." -> thanked
      add aff 1
    > "I'll put in a good word with the captain." -> goodword
  node thanked quill "Don't thank me. Thank the deck for not eating it. And clerk? Don't tell her I lost it."
  node goodword quill "Put in a good word for yourself. You'll need it more. And not a word about the spyglass."
  node ahead quill "Fog, then the Straits. Then whatever's been emptying ships out there. The insurers call it weather."
    > "And you?" -> you
    > "Good to know." -> bye
  node you quill "I call it rude. Weather doesn't take the crew and leave the dinner on the stove. But I'm only the lookout. For now."
    > "For now?" -> ambition
    > "Good to know." -> bye
  node ambition quill "Our navigator died last winter. Somebody has to read the stars. Might as well be somebody who can see them."
    > "Good luck." -> bye
  node bye quill "Off you go. And stop standing like that. You're making the mast nervous."
  # Pell's sextant, given with the captain's terms in hand (rooms.ts, marrow_deck).
  node sextant narrator "She takes the sextant in both hands, the way you hold something that might be taken back."
    -> swear
  node swear quill "Pell's. …You want me to swear to your line."
    > "I want the captain to hear it from a navigator." -> lookout
    > "I want somebody to check my sums. You seem the type." -> sums
  node sums quill "I am the type. But Vane won't take a lookout's word on the reef, and I'm a lookout."
    > "Not in the log, you're not." -> write
      add aff 1
    > "You're the best eyes on this ship." -> eyes
  node lookout quill "I'm a lookout."
    > "Not in the log, you're not." -> write
      add aff 1
    > "You're the best eyes on this ship." -> eyes
  node write narrator "I open the Marrow's log at today's page and write, in my best customs hand: “Quill, navigator.”"
    -> stupid
  node stupid quill "That's the stupidest thing I've ever heard."
    -> underline
  node underline quill "…Underline it."
    -> sight
  node eyes quill "I know. It's nice to hear it from somebody with handwriting."
    -> sight
  node sight narrator "She brings the sun down to the horizon in the mirror, reads it off twice, and lays the figures on my father's line. They agree with it."
    -> sworn
  node sworn quill "The Old Nail lines up with the gap, and your needle lines up with the Old Nail. I'll swear to it. Tell the captain she has a navigator."
    > "I'll tell her." -> END
      take sextant
      set quill_navigator
    > "Tell her yourself. You've earned the look on her face." -> earned
      take sextant
      set quill_navigator
      add aff 1
  node earned quill "I'll tell her. You tell the bosun. He likes you better; you haven't stepped on his feet yet."
  # On the quarterdeck, once she's navigator.
  node nav quill "Navigator. It says so in the log, in a clerk's hand, so it must be true."
    > "Will you show me the stars?" if not night_watch -> tonight
    > "You've been crying." if vane_convinced -> salt
    > "What happens at the reef?" if not vane_convinced -> reef
    > "Carry on, navigator." -> carry
  node tonight quill "Tonight. I keep the watch from the crow's nest now. Climb the shrouds when it's dark, and bring your stomach. You'll want it back."
    > "It's a date. …A watch. It's a watch." -> carry
  node reef quill "If the captain says yes, I steer and you stand at the bow shouting at a compass. If she says no, we go the long way and nobody ever finds out if you were right."
    > "Then she'll have to say yes." -> carry
  node salt quill "It's the sextant. It's got salt in it. …Get to the bow, cargo. I'll be on the wheel."
  node carry quill "Go on. I've a sky to check, and it's bigger than you."
